# blast — Environment Variables Template
# Copy to `.env` and fill in keys you need. Most are OPTIONAL.
# Source `.env` before running blast (e.g., `set -a; source .env; set +a`).
#
# Auto-loaded by:
#   - blast-llm-bridge MCP server (reads BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU directly)
#   - Spike drivers in .priv/research/spike-*/ (jury runs, benchmarks)
#   - Validation agents when invoking jury composition (HYBRID, JURY_3_FLASH3)

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH — Anthropic
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# blast uses Claude Code CLI for all Anthropic calls (subscription-based).
# You do NOT need ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for normal blast use — Claude Code
# authenticates via your subscription.
#
# Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ONLY if you want to:
#   - Run spike drivers standalone (programmatic Anthropic API access)
#   - Future unified dispatcher with direct API
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH — Google Gemini (REQUIRED for JURY_3_FLASH3 composition)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Used by:
#   - JURY_3_FLASH3 composition in `security` (always), `validate-design`
#     (when validation fires), `review --debate` for high-stakes PRs
#   - .priv/research/spike-3/ driver (head-to-head jury experiments)
# Without this, JURY_3_FLASH3 silently degrades to N=2 (Opus + qwen3.6 only).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH — DeepSeek API (OPTIONAL — future jury extension)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a key: https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# Reserved for future N=4 jury composition (4 different LLM providers).
# Currently unused — set only if you want to experiment.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTH — OpenRouter (OPTIONAL — future unified gateway)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Reserved for future unified cloud LLM dispatcher (~100 models via single key).
# Currently unused.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL — Ollama endpoint (REQUIRED if using qwen/local models)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# blast-llm-bridge MCP server reads this on startup. Adjust to your hardware.
# See `.blast/knowledge/references/multi-llm-setup.md` for Ollama setup.
BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU=http://192.168.5.60:11434

# Second Ollama host (Win11/4090) — parallel debate juror in dual-GPU local juries.
# The bridge defaults to this value even if unset; override only if the IP differs.
# BLAST_OLLAMA_WIN11=http://192.168.5.70:11434

# Bridge call timeout in seconds (READ budget). With streaming this is an inter-chunk
# timeout, so a progressing generation is fine; a stalled one aborts after this.
BLAST_LLM_TIMEOUT_S=240
# Connect timeout — surfaces a dead Ollama host in seconds instead of waiting the full read budget.
BLAST_LLM_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_S=5
# Retries on transient faults (ConnectError / timeout / HTTP 5xx). 4xx is never retried.
BLAST_LLM_MAX_RETRIES=2

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OLLAMA SERVER TUNING (host-side — set on the machine RUNNING ollama, not read by blast)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are `ollama serve` env vars (systemd override or shell before `ollama serve`).
# They are the §3.5 / §9 "Ollama hygiene" levers — meaningful speed/VRAM wins:
#
#   OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0     # ~half the KV-cache VRAM, negligible quality loss →
#                                 # lets num_ctx grow (bridge asks for 32k on the coder).
#   OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1      # faster attention, lower memory. Enable on the 5090/4090.
#   OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=3         # concurrent requests per model — REQUIRED for parallel-wave
#                                 # impl to actually run local generation concurrently
#                                 # (unset → calls serialize on the GPU; §4 / impl.md note).
#   OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=-1          # keep models resident (the bridge also pins per-tool);
#                                 # avoids per-call reload latency for the resident pair.
#   OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2    # qwen3-coder + lfm2.5 co-resident (22.1G < 32G); do NOT
#                                 # raise during impl — loading a 3rd model evicts the pair.
#
# Speculative decoding: Ollama has NONE (mid-2026); and it gives ~0 gain on A3B-MoE models
# like qwen3.6 anyway — do not chase it. For heavy concurrent local fan-out (jury), vLLM's
# prefix cache + continuous batching wins; for the single-stream TDD loop, stay on Ollama.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT NEEDS WHAT (quick reference)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Plain blast pipeline (init→requirements→design→tasks→impl→complete)
#     → ZERO env vars. Claude Code handles all auth via subscription.
#     → security audit uses the jury (JURY_3_FLASH3) only on HIGH-STAKES specs
#       (security_critical / risk=high / sensitive paths) — §2 change. There,
#       GEMINI_API_KEY is recommended (without it: degrades to 2-juror). Normal
#       specs run solo Sentinel + the deterministic blast-secscan.py Phase-1 scan.
#
#   `validate-impl` / `validate-tasks` (HYBRID — Sonnet ‖ qwen3.6 → Haiku judge)
#     fires by DEFAULT when --validate flag triggers them.
#     → BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU only.
#     → To opt-out (use solo Sonnet instead): pass `--no-debate` flag.
#
#   `validate-design` / `review` for high-stakes specs (JURY_3_FLASH3)
#     → BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU + GEMINI_API_KEY.
#
#   `--research` flag (research debate via HYBRID)
#     → BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU only.
#     → To opt-out: `--no-debate` (solo Sonnet research, current legacy behavior).
#
#   Privacy mode (`spec.json.privacy: local-only`)
#     → BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU only. Cloud keys are blocked by privacy-gate hook
#       even if set in environment.
#
#   Spike reproduction (.priv/research/spike-*/)
#     → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (or run via Claude Code CLI subprocess) +
#       GEMINI_API_KEY + BLAST_OLLAMA_UBUNTU.
